%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1730d673d6a89a14da4f33af4776de41, type: 3}
  m_Name: SceneTransitionSettings
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SceneTransitionSettings
  fadeOutSeconds: 0.35
  fadeInSeconds: 0.6
  minimumLoadingSeconds: 0.75
  backgroundColor: {r: 0.04, g: 0.05, b: 0.06, a: 1}
  backgroundArt: {fileID: 21300000, guid: af7982fe9be5f2345b90dbf393a6e428, type: 3}
  accentColor: {r: 0.85, g: 0.655, b: 0.353, a: 1}
  tips:
  - Whatever you carry out of a raid is yours. Whatever you carry when it collapses is not.
  - Your safe pocket keeps what's in it, even when a raid goes wrong.
  - Raid modifiers are crafted at home. Bring one to change what waits on the other side.
  - The woods shift between visits. Caches and creatures are rarely where you left them.
  destinations:
  - scene: Raid_MistyWoods
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 39b3f070ceb162144a176a8ff6f9008f, type: 3}
    tips:
    - Whatever you carry out of a raid is yours. Whatever you carry when it collapses is not.
    - Your safe pocket keeps what's in it, even when a raid goes wrong.
    - The woods shift between visits. Caches and creatures are rarely where you left them.
    - Listen. Most creatures give themselves away before the blow lands.
    - When a warning on the ground turns pale, raise your guard. That is a parry.
    - Parry, roll behind it, strike. There is no better blow, but a creature learns a trick it sees too often.
    - A heavy bag slows you, tires you and is heard from far off.
    - Picking a lock is loud. See to whatever is close first.
    - Feel the ground shake? The old troll walks its round. Best let it pass.
    - An exit has to be lit, then held. Light one with time to spare.
  - scene: Raid_TrollValley
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: de7ec80d00a4d5f49a908925d1de0e06, type: 3}
    tips:
    - Whatever you carry out of a raid is yours. Whatever you carry when it collapses is not.
    - Your safe pocket keeps what's in it, even when a raid goes wrong.
    - 'The valley runs one way: up from its mouth to its head. The river comes down it, and the ways out lie up the valley.'
    - Old stone bridges cross the river. Trolls take a toll on them. A ford is slower, and wet, but nobody stands on it.
    - Deep water carries a heavy bag badly. Cross where the river is shallow.
    - The great stones of the valley were trolls once, caught by the dawn. Not all of them are sleeping.
    - Trolls see poorly but hear well. A quiet step gets you past most of them.
    - A troll's blow breaks bones. Parry it and it staggers, which is when it is worth hitting.
    - Something walks the valley's head that is bigger than any troll. Best not wake it.
    - An exit has to be lit, then held. Light one with time to spare.
  - scene: SafeHaven
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d2b678a6222f9854aaff042948eef105, type: 3}
    tips:
    - Stations keep working while you are away. Fill their queues before you leave.
    - Crops grow while you raid. Plant before you go.
    - Give someone a job and they earn their keep while you are gone.
    - Press ({key:Haven}) to run the Haven from anywhere in it.
    - Your journal ({key:Journal}) holds the old stories, your quests, what you know of each creature and how things work.
    - Purified Essence empowers gear and buys skill ranks at the altar.
    - A good meal goes through the portal with you.
    - After dark, wolves prowl just beyond the light. Keep your fires lit.
    - When the bell tolls, a breach is coming. Mend what you can and stand ready.
  - scene: Prologue_MistyWoods
    art: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 723003f4fc14723478de8ae61dbb39d2, type: 3}
    tips:
    - 'Raise your guard just before a blow lands and it is a parry: no damage, and the attacker staggers.'
    - A warning on the ground fills as a blow winds up. When it is full, the blow lands.
    - Roll through a blow at the last moment and you are owed a counter.
    - 'Talk to a companion to give them orders: follow, stay, defend or fall back.'
